Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

[changed subject since this has nothing to do with triangle]

I'm OK with a "numeric" generalization of integer and double, but
this behavior seems sub-optimal:

   > is.integer(1)
   [1] FALSE

   > x <- as.integer(1)

   > is.integer(x)
   [1] TRUE

   > class(x)
   [1] "integer"

   > class(as.integer(1) + as.integer(2))
   [1] "integer"

And this is where it differs from C / Python / Java:

   > as.integer(2) / as.integer(3)
   [1] 0.6666667

Division implicitly converts integers back to generic "numeric"s.

- Bob

