From ucab04b8f0759c712 at groups.google.com  Tue Dec 17 05:39:38 2013
From: ucab04b8f0759c712 at groups.google.com (Daniel Lee)
Date: Tue, 17 Dec 2013 05:39:38 +0000
Subject: Changing how groups of tests run
Message-ID: <7S2FMAjiwc0.7FUd4tZy19sJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/7S2FMAjiwc0/m/7FUd4tZy19sJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Would anyone be opposed to changing how groups of tests currently run? Here is what I propose:

To run any tests in a subdirectory, use that subdirectory as a target. For example, to run all the tests in src/test/mcmc/hmc/hamiltonians, it would look like:
    make src/test/mcmc/hmc/hamiltonians

This would run the three tests in that folder:
  - test/mcmc/hmc/hamiltonians/dense_e_metric
  - test/mcmc/hmc/hamiltonians/diag_e_metric
  - test/mcmc/hmc/hamiltonians/unit_e_metric

If you ran it from a folder one level up, like:
    make src/test/mcmc/hmc

It would run these tests:
  - test/mcmc/hmc/base_hmc
  - test/mcmc/hmc/base_nuts
  - test/mcmc/hmc/base_static_hmc
  - test/mcmc/hmc/hamiltonians/dense_e_metric
  - test/mcmc/hmc/hamiltonians/diag_e_metric
  - test/mcmc/hmc/hamiltonians/unit_e_metric
  - test/mcmc/hmc/hamiltonians/unit_e_metric

I finally figured out how to write a single rule to do all of that work. The next step after this change would be to create folders like src/test/unit, src/test/integration, etc. and I'd populate them with the appropriate tests.

I would leave the location of the built tests alone. That is, src/test/mcmc/base_hmc_test.cpp's executable is created at test/mcmc/base_hmc.

If no one objects, I'll make those changes. If you have a better suggestion, please let me know. I'll take silence as acceptance and create a pull request tomorrow if there are no objections.

Daniel

